<i>I just wanna play my music</i>

966
01:00:19.950 --> 01:00:22.703
<i>All night long</i>

967
01:00:23.829 --> 01:00:24.997
Yeah!

968
01:00:41.263 --> 01:00:43.057
Man. they loved it. You were right.

969
01:00:43.140 --> 01:00:45.476
I know I was right. What did I do?

970
01:00:45.559 --> 01:00:49.021
Not you. Shane.
The label has to let us do this.

971
01:00:49.104 --> 01:00:51.190
They won't. Look at what they made us
call the band.

972
01:00:51.273 --> 01:00:53.901
Yeah! How can we do that?

973
01:00:54.235 --> 01:00:56.445
If we hit the studio tonight. we can
get them a demo by tomorrow.

974
01:00:56.529 --> 01:00:57.988
I mean. they can't say no
once they hear this.

975
01:00:58.072 --> 01:00:59.156
They can't?

976
01:00:59.240 --> 01:01:02.785
Guys. I can't just leave.
I'm not finished here yet.

977
01:01:02.868 --> 01:01:04.495
All right. man. Do what you gotta do.

978
01:01:04.578 --> 01:01:06.539
We are talking about finishing
my birdhouse. right?

979
01:01:06.622 --> 01:01:09.667
- Come on! See you at Final Jam.
- Bye.

980
01:01:11.919 --> 01:01:13.504
...off the chain. That was so great.

981
01:01:13.838 --> 01:01:16.841
That was the best song ever.
It was so great.

982
01:01:16.924 --> 01:01:19.885
- That was so amazing. And...
- I know. he was so...

983
01:01:20.261 --> 01:01:21.345
Did you see them?

984
01:01:21.428 --> 01:01:24.932
Hey. Mitchie.
Tell us about your mom again.

985
01:01:26.141 --> 01:01:30.604
Her mom is a great person.
What's your mom like?

986
01:01:31.355 --> 01:01:32.940
She's like a mom.

987
01:01:34.483 --> 01:01:38.904
I mean. I know she's the president
of Hot Tunes TV China.

988
01:01:39.405 --> 01:01:42.366
but tell me again about
how important she is.

989
01:01:42.449 --> 01:01:43.701
She...

990
01:01:45.202 --> 01:01:46.787
I'm sorry. What?

991
01:01:48.789 --> 01:01:50.541
She's pretty cool.

992
01:01:51.208 --> 01:01:52.376
And...

993
01:01:54.587 --> 01:02:00.634
And she's not the president
of Hot Tunes TV China.

994
01:02:01.635 --> 01:02:05.472
What's that? She's not president?

995
01:02:06.307 --> 01:02:08.976
You mean. you lied to everybody?

996
01:02:09.351 --> 01:02:10.394
No. I was...

997
01:02:10.477 --> 01:02:13.856
So. she's what? A vice president?
Treasurer?

998
01:02:13.939 --> 01:02:15.024
Tess.

999
01:02:15.149 --> 01:02:18.986
Shut up. Go on. Tell us.

1000
01:02:20.988 --> 01:02:22.072
No.

1001
01:02:23.324 --> 01:02:25.993
- She's a cook.
- A cook?

1002
01:02:27.578 --> 01:02:29.663
At Hot Tunes China.

1003
01:02:30.372 --> 01:02:31.582
No.

1004
01:02:32.791 --> 01:02:33.918
Here.

1005
01:02:35.085 --> 01:02:36.545
So you lied.

1006
01:02:37.504 --> 01:02:40.674
Your mom cooks our food.
and you help her.

1007
01:02:41.717 --> 01:02:44.386
That's the only way you could
afford this camp. right?

1008
01:02:44.470 --> 01:02:46.555
You're a real jerk.

1009
01:02:46.639 --> 01:02:50.267
Maybe. But at least
I'm not a big. fat liar.

1010
01:02:51.518 --> 01:02:53.062
Come on. guys.

1011
01:02:53.145 --> 01:02:54.355
Mitchie.

1012
01:02:55.522 --> 01:02:58.567
Mitchie has dishes to do. Let's go.

1013
01:03:00.778 --> 01:03:01.779
Shane.

1014
01:03:01.862 --> 01:03:03.656
- You were lying all summer?
- Yes. but I...

1015
01:03:03.739 --> 01:03:06.367
You know. I'm so used to
people pretending around me.

1016
01:03:06.450 --> 01:03:09.578
- I was not pretending!
- And I really thought you were different.

1017
01:03:09.662 --> 01:03:11.330
But you're just like everyone else.

1018
01:03:11.413 --> 01:03:14.792
You wanted to be friends
with Shane Gray. not me.

1019
01:03:14.875 --> 01:03:17.503
- Trick's on me. huh?
- I was just trying...

1020
01:03:17.586 --> 01:03:21.048
Save it for your interview
with <i>Pop Informer</i> magazine.

1021
01:03:21.715 --> 01:03:23.842
I know I gave you an earful.

1022
01:03:26.679 --> 01:03:28.847
Not here. you don't. Come on.

1023
01:03:47.616 --> 01:03:49.827
So what exactly happened last night?

1024
01:03:49.910 --> 01:03:51.328
Nothing.

1025
01:03:51.412 --> 01:03:54.999
Didn't look like nothing to me. mate.
You look crushed.

1026
01:03:55.082 --> 01:03:57.751
Pummeled. Absolutely destroyed.

1027
01:03:57.835 --> 01:03:59.712
I got it. Uncle Brown.

1028
01:04:00.379 --> 01:04:02.172
Look. whatever.

1029
01:04:02.923 --> 01:04:06.135
I'm just gonna focus on my music.
Change my sound.

1030
01:04:06.218 --> 01:04:09.763
I don't wanna get sidetracked
with liking someone anyway.

1031
01:04:10.931 --> 01:04:13.100
You still looking for that girl?

1032
01:04:13.183 --> 01:04:14.268
What?

1033
01:04:14.435 --> 01:04:17.104
I'm plugged into the
camp gossip. mate.

1034
01:04:17.980 --> 01:04:21.108
It's crazy.
I have her song stuck in my head.

1035
01:04:21.692 --> 01:04:24.361
<i>This is real
This is me</i>

1036
01:04:24.445 --> 01:04:28.532
<i>I'm exactly where
I'm supposed to be now</i>

1037
01:04:28.615 --> 01:04:30.617
<i>Gonna let the light</i>

1038
01:04:44.965 --> 01:04:47.092
"This is real. this is me.

1039
01:04:47.176 --> 01:04:49.970
"I'm exactly where I'm supposed to be.

1040
01:04:50.054 --> 01:04:52.639
"Gonna let the light shine on me."

1041
01:04:59.438 --> 01:05:02.858
Mitchie. you are so never
going to see Final Jam.

1042
01:05:15.412 --> 01:05:17.247
What a joke.

1043
01:05:22.002 --> 01:05:25.672
"I hope you
don't misunderstand. I'm just too cool."

1044
01:05:25.756 --> 01:05:28.926
You know? I mean.
"I'm like too over you."

1045
01:05:29.009 --> 01:05:30.844
You know what I mean?

1046
01:05:31.720 --> 01:05:34.098
Hey. guys. Have a seat.

1047
01:05:39.686 --> 01:05:42.523
So. Final Jam is coming up.
and I know you're all very excited.

1048
01:05:42.606 --> 01:05:45.025
Yeah! You know it!

1049
01:05:46.110 --> 01:05:47.945
So here's some advice.

1050
01:05:50.364 --> 01:05:52.616
It's not all about your image.

1051
01:05:53.659 --> 01:05:57.538
None of it means anything unless
people see who you really are.

1052
01:05:59.164 --> 01:06:02.042
And your music has to be
who you really are.

1053
01:06:03.335 --> 01:06:07.297
It's gotta show how you feel.
Or it doesn't mean anything.

1054
01:06:12.719 --> 01:06:15.556
I didn't know you felt so ashamed
of yourself.

1055
01:06:15.639 --> 01:06:17.349
I'm not ashamed.

1056
01:06:17.432 --> 01:06:21.145
It's just. for once. I just wanted
to fit in and be popular.

1057
01:06:21.228 --> 01:06:24.314
What do you mean?
You have plenty of friends at home.

1058
01:06:24.398 --> 01:06:28.193
I have one. And the last time I checked.
no one was busting their butts

1059
01:06:28.277 --> 01:06:32.030
to sit next to us at the lunch table.
And when I got here I just...

1060
01:06:32.114 --> 01:06:36.285
I just wanted it to be different.
You know? Just once.

1061
01:06:38.829 --> 01:06:42.291
My sweetie. you are so much
more than you can see.

1062
01:06:42.374 --> 01:06:45.460
You don't have to lie about
who or what you are.

1063
01:06:46.378 --> 01:06:49.173
I'm not just saying it
'cause I'm your mom!

1064
01:06:49.548 --> 01:06:50.591
Mom.

1065
01:06:51.091 --> 01:06:53.760
Okay. I admit I'm a little bit biased.

1066
01:06:54.052 --> 01:06:57.556
But it is so true. You are talented.

1067
01:06:57.931 --> 01:07:01.435
Your music speaks to people.
People wanna listen to you.

1068
01:07:01.518 --> 01:07:03.979
And it is not just me and your dad.

1069
01:07:07.691 --> 01:07:09.776
That's what I said.

1070
01:07:12.613 --> 01:07:15.574
- That was funny.
- I know. I want to do that.

1071
01:07:19.703 --> 01:07:22.122
Hey. guys. Can I sit with you?

1072
01:07:25.042 --> 01:07:28.295
I guess.
But you have to give me your cake.

1073
01:07:29.171 --> 01:07:30.547
Okay. deal.

1074
01:07:32.799 --> 01:07:35.552
You know. sitting with the kitchen help
is really hurting my rep.

1075
01:07:35.636 --> 01:07:36.929
What rep?

1076
01:07:39.431 --> 01:07:42.226
Believe me. it's probably not that funny.

1077
01:07:47.689 --> 01:07:49.900
The chicken was kind of dry.

1078
01:07:49.983 --> 01:07:53.528
Could you tell your mom to be
just a little more careful?

1079
01:07:53.904 --> 01:07:55.155
Tess!

1080
01:07:57.783 --> 01:08:01.787
Stop talking to me like that.
Stop talking to everyone like that.

1081
01:08:02.246 --> 01:08:05.123
I may be the cook's daughter.
and my father may not be rich.

1082
01:08:05.207 --> 01:08:08.293
but I'm a much better person than
someone who feels good about herself

1083
01:08:08.377 --> 01:08:11.129
because she makes everyone
else feel bad.

1084
01:08:11.213 --> 01:08:13.090
And I'll take that any day.

1085
01:08:13.173 --> 01:08:16.343
If it wasn't obvious.
you're so out of the group.

1086
01:08:21.181 --> 01:08:23.392
Then we'll make our own group.

1087
01:09:40.010 --> 01:09:43.680
- I don't know why this is so fascinating.
- I don't think you're doing that right.

1088
01:09:43.764 --> 01:09:47.184
- Wait. Look. I'm a pro.
- Don't get it in my macaroni.

1089
01:09:47.267 --> 01:09:48.685
I'm sure they have it!

1090
01:09:48.769 --> 01:09:51.188
Okay. she has officially lost it.

1091
01:09:51.271 --> 01:09:54.274
No. I didn't lose anything.
You guys stole it.

1092
01:09:55.025 --> 01:09:56.777
- What?
- What's going on here?

1093
01:09:56.860 --> 01:10:01.281
Tess thinks that Mitchie and Caitlyn
stole her charm bracelet.

1094
01:10:01.365 --> 01:10:02.366
What?

1095
01:10:02.449 --> 01:10:05.369
I'm sorry. Brown. but these girls
would never do such a thing.

1096
01:10:05.452 --> 01:10:07.954
Yeah. Look. let's just settle this. right?

1097
01:10:08.038 --> 01:10:09.039
But...

1098
01:10:09.122 --> 01:10:12.709
I know it was her. She was lying
all summer about who she is.

1099
01:10:12.793 --> 01:10:14.419
Who knows what else she'd lie about?

1100
01:10:14.503 --> 01:10:17.756
- Now. wait a minute.
- Mom. don't.

1101
01:10:18.382 --> 01:10:20.300
If she wants to look. let her.
This is stupid.

1102
01:10:20.384 --> 01:10:23.595
Okay. look. let me just scope this out.

1103
01:10:23.678 --> 01:10:26.723
and then I'll have a quick look
in your cabin. Right?

1104
01:10:26.807 --> 01:10:28.392
- Fine.
- Whatever.

1105
01:10:31.478 --> 01:10:34.648
You're not gonna find anything.
'cause I didn't...

1106
01:10:43.323 --> 01:10:45.992
That's it. That is my charm bracelet.

1107
01:10:46.076 --> 01:10:47.702
There's gotta be some mistake.

1108
01:10:47.786 --> 01:10:49.830
Like what?
I snuck into the kitchen and...

1109
01:10:49.913 --> 01:10:52.707
Tess. I got this. All right?

1110
01:10:53.417 --> 01:10:55.669
I am totally wigged-out.

1111
01:10:56.294 --> 01:10:57.921
Yeah. So are we.

1112
01:10:58.004 --> 01:10:59.214
I'm not.

1113
01:11:02.008 --> 01:11:04.428
Well. rules are rules.

1114
01:11:05.178 --> 01:11:07.889
and since it's the end of camp.
I have no choice.

1115
01:11:07.973 --> 01:11:11.560
I've gotta ban you guys
from the rest of camp activities.

1116
01:11:11.643 --> 01:11:14.688
until the end of Final Jam.

1117
01:11:14.771 --> 01:11:17.107
We didn't do anything. She's lying.

1118
01:11:17.190 --> 01:11:19.234
- Do you have any proof?
- No. but...

1119
01:11:19.317 --> 01:11:22.529
Well. then I'm sorry. My hands are tied.

1120
01:11:26.491 --> 01:11:29.578
Until the end of Final Jam.

1121
01:11:47.554 --> 01:11:50.390
Camper mates. and matettes.

1122
01:11:50.474 --> 01:11:53.560
I am holding the lineup for Final Jam.

1123
01:11:53.643 --> 01:11:56.438
I am gonna pin it up on the wall.

1124
01:11:56.521 --> 01:12:00.525
Let me get out of the room before
you all come and have a look at it.

1125
01:12:00.609 --> 01:12:02.569
All right! Goodness me.

1126
01:12:04.654 --> 01:12:05.989
This is so not fair.

1127
01:12:06.072 --> 01:12:07.240
I know.

1128
01:12:09.242 --> 01:12:10.619
Guess who?

1129
01:12:10.702 --> 01:12:11.661
Dude. you're in the room.
I can see you.

1130
01:12:11.745 --> 01:12:13.705
I can see you. too. man.

1131
01:12:14.498 --> 01:12:15.957
I've missed you.

1132
01:12:16.041 --> 01:12:17.334
Group hug.

1133
01:12:18.376 --> 01:12:21.880
Much better. It hasn't been
the same just hugging Nate.

1134
01:12:22.255 --> 01:12:24.049
Yeah. it hasn't been.

1135
01:12:24.799 --> 01:12:26.343
So. good news.

1136
01:12:26.426 --> 01:12:28.303
The press is here and they're gonna
cover the whole night.

1137
01:12:28.386 --> 01:12:30.931
- The label loves it.
- That's awesome!

1138
01:12:31.014 --> 01:12:34.559
Hey. man. where's this amazing singer
you've been looking for?

1139
01:12:34.643 --> 01:12:36.436
What? I know things.

1140
01:12:37.354 --> 01:12:39.439
Hoping to find her tonight.

1141
01:12:44.402 --> 01:12:47.113
This was supposed to be a fun summer
that was all about music.

1142
01:12:47.197 --> 01:12:50.242
and all I did was get caught up
in Tess drama.

1143
01:12:50.909 --> 01:12:52.285
It happens.

1144
01:12:52.619 --> 01:12:55.372
I can't believe I agreed to be
some background singer

1145
01:12:55.455 --> 01:12:57.415
just because I got intimidated.

1146
01:12:57.499 --> 01:12:59.793
That's what Tess can do to you.

1147
01:12:59.960 --> 01:13:02.879
No. I did it to me.

1148
01:13:03.713 --> 01:13:06.550
I've never seen Brown so harsh.

1149
01:13:07.467 --> 01:13:09.219
I know. He just kept repeating

1150
01:13:09.302 --> 01:13:11.721
"Until the end of Final Jam."

1151
01:13:12.722 --> 01:13:14.849
I know. I was there.

1152
01:13:19.396 --> 01:13:20.605
What?

1153
01:13:21.314 --> 01:13:22.566
What?

1154
01:13:22.816 --> 01:13:24.943
Come on! Let's go! Let's go!

1155
01:13:33.326 --> 01:13:37.581
<i>Okay. Who's stoked? Yeah!</i>

1156
01:13:39.624 --> 01:13:41.835
<i>All right! All right!</i>

1157
01:13:43.545 --> 01:13:44.588
Yeah!

1158
01:13:44.671 --> 01:13:51.261
<i>Okay. campers. friends. family.
Camp Rock fans. this is it.</i>

1159
01:13:51.344 --> 01:13:54.264
<i>Tonight music history will be made</i>

1160
01:13:54.347 --> 01:13:59.436
<i>as Camp Rock finds
a new Final Jam winner!</i>

1161
01:14:02.230 --> 01:14:04.441
Five. six. seven. eight.

1162
01:14:04.524 --> 01:14:06.985
<i>Come on.
come on. come on</i>

1163
01:14:07.068 --> 01:14:08.361
<i>Look at me</i>

1164
01:14:10.697 --> 01:14:13.700
This is not amateur night.
This is serious.

1165
01:14:13.783 --> 01:14:14.784
We did it right!

1166
01:14:14.868 --> 01:14:18.538
No! You didn't. You never do!
I'm trying to win here.

1167
01:14:18.622 --> 01:14:21.041
You guys may be used to losing.
but not me.

1168
01:14:21.124 --> 01:14:23.084
I'm tired of picking up the slack.

1169
01:14:23.168 --> 01:14:25.462
Stop telling us what to do!

1170
01:14:25.545 --> 01:14:26.838
You're the one
who's ruining everything.

1171
01:14:26.921 --> 01:14:29.007
You're too intense all the time.

1172
01:14:29.090 --> 01:14:32.969
and I am sick and tired
of picking up your slack. too!

1173
01:14:33.053 --> 01:14:34.929
Peggy. come back here!

1174
01:14:38.224 --> 01:14:40.852
Who needs her?
She was holding us back.

1175
01:14:41.519 --> 01:14:43.730
Now you really better not mess up.

1176
01:14:43.813 --> 01:14:48.234
You know what? Don't worry about me.
Do it yourself. I'm done.

1177
01:14:49.611 --> 01:14:54.240
BTW. your lip gloss is
so not glossy anymore.

1178
01:14:56.534 --> 01:14:57.911
All right.

1179
01:14:58.411 --> 01:15:04.250
<i>This year. the Final Jam winner
will not only get a Camp Rock trophy</i>

1180
01:15:04.334 --> 01:15:06.294
<i>and a big one. I might add.</i>

1181
01:15:06.378 --> 01:15:09.756
<i>he or she is gonna get a sweet prize.</i>

1182
01:15:09.839 --> 01:15:15.595
<i>a chance to record with my nephew.
pop star Shane Gray!</i>

1183
01:15:15.679 --> 01:15:20.600
<i>Yes! All right! Give it up! All right!</i>

1184
01:15:21.893 --> 01:15:24.521
<i>To make sure
the right camper is chosen.</i>

1185
01:15:24.604 --> 01:15:28.692
<i>we've invited the other members
of Connect 3 to be judges.</i>

1186
01:15:28.775 --> 01:15:30.026
<i>Yes!</i>

1187
01:15:31.069 --> 01:15:32.737
<i>Thank you so much.</i>

1188
01:15:34.739 --> 01:15:36.116
<i>All right.</i>

1189
01:15:37.617 --> 01:15:40.954
<i>Okay. Put your hands together
for Barron James.</i>

1190
01:15:41.037 --> 01:15:45.083
<i>Sander Lawyer. and
the Hasta La Vista Crew.</i>

1191
01:15:50.964 --> 01:15:53.299
<i>Yeah. it's your boy Barry</i>

1192
01:15:54.676 --> 01:15:58.304
<i>And the place to be is crazy
Come rock with me</i>

1193
01:15:59.472 --> 01:16:01.766
<i>Couldn't wait to leave
But now I hate to go</i>

1194
01:16:01.850 --> 01:16:04.144
<i>Last day at camp
Packing my bags slow</i>

1195
01:16:04.227 --> 01:16:06.646
<i>Made so many friends
Why does it have to end</i>

1196
01:16:06.730 --> 01:16:09.441
<i>In the end it's a win
'Cause we grown so close together</i>

1197
01:16:09.524 --> 01:16:11.818
<i>Remember when we first met. first day</i>

1198
01:16:11.901 --> 01:16:13.236
<i>Thinking this would be no fun</i>

1199
01:16:13.319 --> 01:16:14.320
<i>No way
Way</i>

1200
01:16:14.404 --> 01:16:15.530
<i>Now it's time to leave
Leave</i>

1201
01:16:15.613 --> 01:16:16.698
<i>But now we wanna stay
Stay</i>

